<title>USA: Halifax sees profit from office park sale.</title>
<headline>Halifax sees profit from office park sale.</headline>
<dateline>ALEXANDRIA, Va. 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Halifax Corp said Thursday it has agreed to sell its Halifax Office Park in Fairfax County, Virginia, for $5.25 million.</p>
<p>Halifax said the sale will produce &quot;a reasonable profit&quot; and &quot;significantly improve&quot; its balance sheet by cutting overall debt by about $5 million.</p>
<p>The sale requires the buyer to complete an engineering and economic study and obtain suitable financing. If these are achieved, the sale should happen before March 24, 1997, Halifax said.</p>
</text>
